---
description: Rules for migrated code
alwaysApply: true
---
- Represent money with Python's decimal.Decimal. Never use float.
- Match COBOL rounding: fields marked ROUNDED use ROUND_HALF_UP. Others truncate (ROUND_DOWN).
- Keep every business rule from the COBOL, and cite the COBOL line in a comment.
- Never edit the original COBOL files.